  "speaker": "grandma",
  "voiceId": "9c633ca4a45a4e9ba74cb36cfa21fb00",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free",
  "text": "I was spreading a cloth over the garden table when the wind snatched one corner from my hand. I still held the opposite corner, which meant I had a very poor kite and nowhere sensible to put it.\n\nPip helped us find a way to share our stories again. Before I finished this page, I opened the storage beside the bench and brought out the cushions. I set them where people could reach them.\n\nMara fetched four smooth stones from beside the path. We placed one on each corner. I eased my fingers away first. Sol let go next. The cloth lifted a little between the stones, then settled.\n\nKeep the boat’s route clear. When you reach the garden, prepare our planting spot with me, place the seed and cover it with soil. The bridge stays in place so everyone can return.\n\nYou kept your promise, Pip. This flower began with our seed, and now we have a day to remember. Would you like its lantern to show our planting or the stories we shared?\n\nWe can keep our usual time or postpone the gathering until the last boat returns. Choose when we should meet and who will read Mara’s story. Then try your plan.\n\nWe set out our picnic. The wind ruffled our hair and rattled the leaves, but the cloth stayed put. I could finally use both hands to cut the cake.\n\nI kept looking down the path when I should have gone to the dock. Thank you for asking her, Pip. We could start after the last boat returns.\n\nMara sent her story across the river. Please take her this copy of mine, Pip. I’d like her to have something to open when work is done.\n\nSo she was waiting for passengers while I was waiting for her. I wish I’d known. We can work out a way for her story to reach us.\n\nSol, can I ask you something? I used to hear about the things you made. What kept you from bringing stories before today?",
  "textSha256": "be4f7fd5f51ce2c4301baf0d0732df26662a98a196e38f2521c987f421867fbb",
